   Launch the refactor subagent for the loyalty-discount cycle, per `tdd.md`: "After **Green** → launch the `refactor` subagent." The prompt should follow the established pattern — test file `src/claim-office.spec.ts`, implementation file `src/claim-office.ts`, passing tests 18, Green summary: threaded `customer` into `quote` and added the policy-wide 20% loyalty discount (≥2 years) as a negative amount in the `modifierAmounts` list — plus the standing constraints ("rounding must stay in the MHPCO's favour (premiums Math.ceil, payouts Math.floor) and percentage arithmetic must stay in the integer-percent `percentOf` form") and a do-not-implement-ahead note (follow-up contract −15% discount and all claim/payout logic are still `it.todo`). Then continue the cycle with the `red` skill for the next test, "customer with 1 year with MHPCO → no loyalty discount".

